      "content": "You are absolutely right to be concerned about dehumanizing tropes, but the industry standard is not a blanket \"protected\" loophole; it is a strict filter that specifically targets the *intent* to harm and the *target* of the satire. If a joke relies on dehumanizing tropes against a protected group, even if labeled \"satire,\" it is almost universally flagged as hate speech because the mechanism of the joke itself is the harm. Your guidelines must explicitly state that the *method* of the joke matters just as much as the *label*, ensuring that content designed to mock or degrade specific groups is caught regardless of its comedic framing.",
